(1) This ordinance is designed and intended to protect the health, safety and general welfare of the public while balancing the interests of the residents of the city, telecommunications providers, and telecommunications customers. It seeks to do so by establishing guidelines for the siting of all wireless, cellular, television and radio telecommunications towers and antennae within the incorporated limits of the city.
(2) The goals of this ordinance are:
a. To encourage the design and construction of communication towers and antennae to minimize adverse visual and residential impacts;
b. To minimize the total number of communication towers within the community necessary to provide adequate personal wireless services to residents of the city;
c. To encourage the location of communication towers in non-residential areas;
d. To encourage the joint use of new and existing communication tower sites among service providers; and
e. To enhance the ability of the providers of wireless communication services to deliver such services to the community effectively and efficiently.
(Ord. No. 98-12-5, § III, 12-7-98)

